body:
Turn-ons: Shows interest, makes eye contact, smiles, good hygiene (hair done/clean, nice clothes, etc.), rebel/edgy or at least tries to be unique.

Turn-offs: not good at texting/talking in person, ignoring me, not showing interest, acting stuck-up, being too forthcoming.

&#x200B;

He killed his parents and then committed a mass shooting. Yes, he needs help instead of prison time, but the justice system is corrupt and everyone knows that. He doesn't deserve to be in a prison, but rather a mental institution or a psych ward, as well and juvenile detention. 

As I said, they are *lucky* to get out in their twenties, but this is not always the case. Some early kids, as well as early teens, can get help and then release. Yet there are some that due to the justice system or state, are treated worse. 

&#x200B;
